{
	"_about": "Where every piece of art still to be made lands, how big it must be and what in the game shows it, for every open request in docs/24 (A51 on, D344; A32 to A49 in part, D358; the rest from A2, D369). `tools/take_art.py` reads it: `check` says, for each request, what is in DROP-ZONE/<id>/, what is already in place and what is still the stand-in; `take <id>` checks each file's size and moves it to `to`. A file is matched by its name (`name`, without the folder); a PixelLab zip is unpacked first. `size` is [width, height] in pixels; `rotations` is a folder of the eight facings (south.png, south-east.png, ... as art/items/bone_sword); `each` repeats a file for every name in it, `{each}` in `name` and `to`. `prop: false` marks a picture under art/props that is not laid as a prop (the opening draws it). `stand_in` says what shows until the art is in, `shows` where it is seen and what reads it, so nothing but generating is left on the day. `also` names earlier requests a file answers too (A58's pictures are A10 to A25's keepsakes). `set` is a whole body or creature, a folder of states (idle, walk, attack ...), each a folder of facings (idle: the eight facings as pictures; the moves: a folder of frames a heading), taken as it stands; `size` is its idle facing's. `frames` is a folder of numbered frames (frame_000.png ...). `size` \"any\" is not checked. `made_as` names the request that makes a row's pictures (A10 to A25 are A58's). A shows that begins \"Planned\" lands where the game is to read it once that is built.",
